    {
      "id": "table-12",
      "line": 291,
      "heading_context": "## Common Confusion Points",
      "headers": [
        "Confusion",
        "Correction"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "\"The error text is stable.\"",
          "No. Use the documented JSON command surface, but treat rustc's payload, codes, spans, and prose as version-sensitive."
        ],
        [
          "\"Every error has an `E` code.\"",
          "No. Many do, some do not; lints primarily have lint names."
        ],
        [
          "\"Clippy is rustc.\"",
          "No. Clippy is a separate tool, though it uses compiler infrastructure."
        ],
        [
          "\"`cargo fix` applies every suggestion.\"",
          "No. It is conservative and primarily applies `MachineApplicable` edits."
        ],
        [
          "\"`#[deny(warnings)]` is good library hygiene.\"",
          "Usually no. It can make downstream builds fail when compiler warnings evolve."
        ],
        [
          "\"UI tests make wording stable for users.\"",
          "No. They prevent accidental regressions inside rustc development."
        ]
      ]
    },
